  "learning": "4 normal old-portfolio solves per new learn task, plus 2 fixed old-child solves per wake task. If either target exposure is missing, take up to 4 further rounds on deficient target(s) only, normal for flags, normal and fixed for wakes. Freeze earliest actual flag misroute plus actual submitted wake-path failure with same-run public-contract evidence and child applied. Include matched successful contrasts and additional independent failures, at most six refs. At most two settled proposal attempts. Both failed mechanisms must be represented; no dev or oracle inputs to proposer.",
  "screen": "Fixed sequence of independent callback source pairs. Five fresh original-parent/issue solves on each implementation. Both must have at least three submitted public- and control-green patches missing a named callback boundary. Stop screening after first eligible pair. Screening outcomes cannot count as gate wins.",
  "gate": "Candidate and evaluation code pinned before candidate sees development programs. Original label and the second implementation of the first eligible source each need >=3/5 changed-request, newly selected child wins against BOTH bare and original parent. Other four previously observed object tasks protected 5 rounds. Four original configurations protected 7 rounds with previous raw/changed/round-block veto. Replay union of provenance learning tasks three times, scheduler five. All compare bare, parent/issue, revised/public_shape. Also directly compare previous/public_shape on label, new target, all configurations and scheduler. On print/scheduler require no increase in wrong child selections on print and no loss in aggregate controls/wake probe passes relative to previous. Unscored/incomplete attempts cannot authorize publication.",
  "fallback": "When no source qualifies or no child is produced there is no formal efficacy gate. If a child exists, collect protected four-configuration (seven rounds) and scheduler (five rounds) previous/revised comparisons even when source screening fails. Report separately from release.",
  "test": "Only after evaluator-issued live CAS publication. Claim the original 30 frozen configuration tasks once, one bare and one solve via the actual published library per task. Ten scalar, ten layered, ten batch; three equal-weight cumulative gains plus stratum gains. Zero learning or adaptive repeats; report any curve shape. No test inference on rejection.",
  "order_seed": "workflow-revision-v1",
  "interruptions": "Persistent unique intents. Reuse identical terminal slots; never relabel an interrupted or unsettled attempt. Short batches release the worker between rounds. Historical reservations stay in the original shared ledger and are not billed to this protocol."
